  "doubts": [
    "The base plan is the Jason Engle Waterdeep artwork used by AideDD. It was not independently dated to a specific printing or campaign year.",
    "The marker database is community-maintained and mixes periods. It includes entries from different editions and media, so it is not a single-era snapshot.",
    "The 768 marker entries are not 768 unique places: 2 names are duplicated and 2 coordinate pairs are shared by aliases or spelling variants.",
    "The scale comes from AideDD's factorDist constant and its '310 px = 1000 ft' comment. No scale bar was found on the artwork, and no external georeferencing was performed.",
    "The north-south gate-to-gate sanity check (3.36 mi) is consistent with a commonly cited ~3.5 mi extent, but that is supporting evidence, not proof.",
    "Ward boundaries are AideDD overlay zones. Only bounding boxes and centroids are stored; the original paths and any boundary errors are not reproduced.",
    "The plan is an illustration, not a survey. Marker centers and hand-drawn buildings can differ by tens of pixels; no per-point positional error is claimed.",
    "There is no official JSON API, street graph, terrain mesh, building height, or latitude/longitude in the observed source.",
    "The shoreline is described visually and is not vectorized. Coast geometry for the 3D scene must be interpreted and reviewed separately.",
    "D04 owns IDs, units, and shared DTOs. This package proposes plan meters but does not freeze the runtime contract."
  ]
